spans.s:
सेवा f. visit, service, attendance, worship, devotion to,
use, practice, employment;
 sexual intercourse with (gen. or —˚).

सेव् से॑वते (से॑व˚ति), pp. सेवित stay by (acc. or
loc.), inhabit, frequent, visit;
 serve, revere, worship;
 attend upon,
devote one's self to (acc.);
 practise, use, employ, enjoy (also
sexually). C. सेवयति serve, worship. — अनु stay or dwell in;
 wait
on, reverence. आ = S. समा devote one's self to (acc.), practise,
use, employ. उप = S. अभ्युप worship, revere. नि (षेवते) stay
in, have intercourse with (loc.);
 inhabit, visit, frequent, etc. = S.
परि (षेवते & सेवते) visit, follow, obey, revere;
 practise, like.
सम् be together, stay at or with, dwell in, frequent, visit etc. = S.
— Cf. निषेवित.

सेवक (—˚) inhabiting, serving, revering, practising;
 m.
inhabitant etc.

सेवितृ a. & m. serving, worshipping, practising;
 servant
etc.
